---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About My Lab Tests"
  description="Who runs My Lab Tests, why it exists, and how it stays independent."
  path="/about/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
>
  <div class="prose-tight max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold sm:text-3xl">About My Lab Tests</h1>
    <p>
      Booking a lab test in India means opening six tabs, decoding six package
      names, and still not knowing if "90 parameters" beats "63 tests". We got
      tired of doing that maths for our families, so we built the site that does
      it for everyone.
    </p>
    <p>
      My Lab Tests compares prices, packages and service quality across India's
      major diagnostics brands, city by city. Prices are re-checked on a nightly
      schedule, package contents are broken down into standard panels, and the
      total you see includes collection fees and live coupons.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">What we are not</h2>
    <p>
      We're not a lab, not a booking agent, and not a medical advisor. When you
      pick an option, you book on the lab's own website — we never handle your
      sample, your payment or your report. And nothing here replaces a doctor:
      test results need clinical context we can't give.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">How we stay independent</h2>
    <p>
      Every lab — big or small — runs through the same automated pipeline, and
      the default sort everywhere is lowest total price. The ranking rules are
      published on our <a href="/editorial-policy/" class="text-navy underline">How we compare</a> page.
      If a lab ever pays us for placement, it will say so on the listing, in
      plain words.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">
      Operating entity, registered address and the name of our medical reviewer
      will be published here before public launch.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
